> how to get the zero-order correlations for my model

Correlations of what?

cov2cor(lavInspect(fit, "sampstat")$cov) # observed correlations (estimated if using FIML)
## model-implied correlations:
lavInspect(fit, "cor.ov") # among observed variables
lavInspect(fit, "cor.lv <http://cor.lv>") # among latent variables
lavInspect(fit, "cor.all") # among observed and latent variables

See the ?lavInspect help page.

> I'm guessing it's one of the outputs from inspect(fit, what = "std"),

No, that is the standardized solution.  If you want to know the correlation matrix of residuals among your model's endogenous variables, you can use cov2cor(lavInspect(fit, "theta"))

Or likewise the residual correlation matrix of latent variables

cov2cor(lavInspect(fit, "std")$psi)

