The same way he did it in the post.

You use the := operator, to create this effect size, using named parameters for the mean differences and variances.

Also, notice that lavaan will estimate the variances, not standard deviations, so you will need to ask for the square root of those. Somtehing like this

Lets say the parameters are named as such in the lavaan model
- MD1 = Mean.difgroup 1
- VR1 (variance)= SD.difgroup 1
- MD2 = Mean.dif group 2
- VR2 (variance)= SD.difgroup 2

EFFECT SIZE = [Mean.difgroup 1/SD.difgroup 1] − [Mean.dif group 2 /SD.difgroup 2] ### this translate into the define parameter EF
EF := (MD1/sqrt(VR1)) - (MD2/sqrt(VR2))

